Shake off.; Excutere.
See <Disperse-Discutere>.

@AC 7418. The evil Spirits shake off there the dust of their feet, when they want to bring anyone to damnation.

@8228. "Jehovah shook off the Egyptians into the midst of the sea" (Exodus 14:27) = that thus they themselves cast themselves into Hell.

@9062. "If he shall strike out the tooth of his servant, or the tooth of his maidservant" (Exodus 21:27) = if he shall destroy truth or the affection thereof in the Sensuous... To "strike out" = to destroy.

@9277[2]. "Thy olive shall be shaken" (Deuteronomy 28:40) = that good will perish. @AE 638[19].

@TCR 656[end]. Would put forth its three gods...

@AE 365[8]. To "shake off the dust of their feet" (Matthew 10:14) = lest what is damned should adhere to them therefrom... Those who belonged to the representative Churches shook off the dust of their feet when the truths of doctrine were not received.

@538[9]. To "smite her wealth in the sea" (Zechariah 9:4) = to cast falsities into Hell.

Shame.; Pudor.
Ashamed, To be.; Pudefieri.

@AC 213. See <Naked>. @AR 213. @706. @AE 244.

@216. To "make themselves belts" = to be affected with shame... Being in natural good, they were affected with shame. @224.

@829. Shame is (thus) insinuated into him. @SE 1696.

@1641[2]. Is shame possible without reverence? @SE 1051.

@2751[end]. On hearing this, he receded with shame.

@4793[4]. The shame of injuring society, an internal bond.

@HH 403[end]. That they might be ashamed.

@506[3]. Some, then, are ashamed; some are not ashamed.

@CL 513[2]. They then practise these things without being withheld by shame.

@SE 3141. See <Fear>. @3149.

@3179. To those suffused with shame, there appears a head nodding, in front.

@3456. (Thus) he was devoid of shame. @4790.

@AE 357[10]. "They shall not be ashamed when they speak with the enemies in the gate" (Psalms 127:5) = that there shall be nothing of fear of evils from the Hells. ( = not to be conquered. @724[10].)

@386[22]. "They shall not be ashamed in the time of evil" (Psalms 37:19) = that they shall conquer when tempted by evils.

@401[20]. The truth of faith and good of love are said to "blush," and "be ashamed," when they are no longer received.

@577[11]. Shame was represented by the hand upon the head. Illustrated.

@654[59]. "The strength of Pharaoh shall be for shame" (Isaiah 30:3) = no faculty of resisting evils from Own intelligence.

@734[18]. To be "ashamed" (Zechariah 10:5) = to yield, being said of those who are overcome.

@811[13]. To "be ashamed, and affected with ignominy" (Jeremiah 22:22) = to be destitute of all good and truth; for when such come among the Angels, they are affected with shame and ignominy.

@1008[2]. Adulteries are (now) practised without shame...

