@AC 939. By a shaving off of the hair, as with swine, they seem to become white.

@3301[4]. "When shaved, his strength departed" (Judges 16:19). Explained. @5247[4]. @DSS 49[3]. @AE 66[2].

@--[5]. "The high priest... should not shave his head" (Leviticus 21:10); and so "the Levites were not to shave their head" (Ezekiel 44:19). Explained. @5247[2]. @9960[5].

@10076[7]. The dissipation of Divine good in the Heavens, is signified by to "shave the head."

@DSS 35[2]. The prophet shaving off the hairs of his head and his beard (Ezekiel 5) represented the state of the Jewish Church as to the Word. Explained.

@AE 66[3]. "The Nazarite was not to shave his hair" (Numbers 6). Explained.

@577[10]. "Not to shave the beard" = not to deprive themselves of what is rational by taking away its ultimate...

Shaveh.; Schaveh.

@AC 1723. "The valley of Shaveh" (Genesis 14:17) = the goods of the external man.

Sheaf.; Manipulus.

@AC 4686. "We were binding sheaves -manipulantes manipulos-" (Genesis 37:7) = teaching from doctrine. "A sheaf" = doctrine.

@--. "Joseph's sheaf" = doctrine from the Lord's Divine truth.

@--[2]. The reason "a sheaf" = doctrine. Explained. Thus a sheaf in which is the crop = doctrine in which is truth.

@--[end]. To "bear sheaves" (Psalms 126:6) = the doctrinals of this truth.

@4687. "My sheaf arose and stood up" (Genesis 37:7) = the doctrinal concerning the Lord's Divine Human (reigning).

@4688. "Your sheaves surrounded" (Genesis 37:7) = those in the faith of some charity.

@--. "The sheaves," here, = all things of doctrine, or all things of faith. Explained.

@4689. "And bowed themselves to my sheaf" (Genesis 37:7) = adoration of the Divine Human.

@5339[2]. "Handfuls," or "collections" = series. (See @5530.)

@9295[2]. "A sheaf" = a series and collection of such things; for truths are disposed in sheaves -manipulatim-.

@--. "Wave the sheaf" (Leviticus 23:11) = vivify the goods of truth.

@9394[5]. Generals disposed as into bundles.

@--. Each bundle in the body consists of many motor fibres.

@10083. "The sheaf of the first-fruits" = the state (of good) collectively.

@10303[4]. The series into which truths (or falsities) are disposed, are signified by "sheaves," and "bundles." Illustrated.

@LJ 70. [Swedenborg footnote 1.] "Sheaves" = the dispositions into series of the truths and falsities with man; thus also [the dispositions into series] of men in whom are truths and falsities. References.

@DP 111[2]. These make as it were one bundle.

Shear.; Tondere. Detondere.
Shearing, A.; Tonsio.
Shearer, A.; Tonsor.

@AC 3703[16]. Purification from falsities is signified by... "she shall poll her head" (Deuteronomy 21:12). @AE 555[16].

@4110. "Laban went to shear his flock" (Genesis 31:19) = a state of use and an end of good... To "shear" = use, thus end. @4853.

@--[3]. That to "shear the flock" = to perform use, is evident from the fact, that in the internal sense, the shearing of the flock is nothing but use; for wool comes thence. Illustrated.

@--. Hence sheep-shearing, and to be near the shearers, was an honourable office. Illustrated.

@4853. "Shearers" (Genesis 38:12) = use; thus to will use, or to consult for. @4857.

@5247. [Joseph] "polled himself" (Genesis 41:14) = rejection and change as to the things of the exterior Natural. To "poll," to wit, the head and beard = to reject such things as are of the exterior Natural; for the hair which was polled = that Natural. Illustrated... Hence those who have been rational appear there with hair becomingly dressed.

@--[2]. "Not to shave the head... but in polling to poll the head" (Ezekiel 44:20) = not to reject the Natural, but to accommodate it to agreement; thus to subordinate it. Illustrated.

@--[4]. On fulfilling his Nazariteship, the Nazarite was to poll his head (Numbers 6:9).

@--[5]. "Jehovah shall shave -detondebit- with a hired razor" (Isaiah 7:20).

@--. "Make thee bald, and shave thyself" (Micah 1:16). @AE 724[12], Explained.

@5569. To cut the hair = to accommodate natural things so that they are becoming.

@9960[3]. To "shave -detondere- the head" (Isaiah 7:20) = to deprive of the internal truths of the Church; to "shave the hair and consume the beard" = to deprive of its external truths. @10044[3].

@AE 66[6]. To "crop the head," to "shave the beard," and to "cause baldness," = to deprive of all truth and good; for he who is deprived of ultimates is also deprived of prior things. Illustrated.

Sheath.; Vagina.

@AC 6816. The Spirits of Mercury do not want to look at the sheath; but at things stripped of their sheath.

Sheba.; Scheba.

