@--[3]. "Sheba" (Isaiah 60:6) = the celestial and spiritual things thence, which are "gold, and frankincense."

@--[4]. Celestial things signified by "Sheba." Enumerated. The Knowledges of such things are properly "Sheba."

@--[end]. "Sheba" = Knowledges and adorations, which are "incense, and calamus" (Jeremiah 6:20); here, those which are devoid of charity.

@1247[end]. Sheba the son of Joktan (Genesis 10:28) is not mentioned elsewhere in the Word.

@3048[5]. "From Sheba" (Isaiah 9) = from the celestial things of love and faith.

@--. "The queen of Sheba coming to Solomon..." (1 Kings 10) = the wisdom and intelligence which came to the Lord.

@3465. "Sheba," in "Beer-Sheba," see <Shibah>.

@9688[3]. "Sheba" = Knowledges.

@9881[end]. "Gold from Sheba" = the good of Knowledges. Illustrated.

@10199[6]. "Sheba and Raamah" (Ezekiel 27:22) = those in the Knowledges of celestial and spiritual things. @10254[5]. @AE 242[13]. @717[10].

@10254[6]. "Sheba" = chiefly those in the Knowledges of celestial things.

@AR 379[6]. "Gold of Sheba" (Psalms 72:15) = wisdom thence, ( = the good of love into which the Lord will lead them by Knowledges. @AE 242[18].) ( = the good of charity. @328[15]. @329[18].)

@AE 242[17]. "Sheba" = where these Knowledges are.

@324[9]. "Sheba" = these Knowledges.

@406[9]. "The kings of Sheba and Seba" (Psalms 72:10) = the interior and exterior goods of the natural man; "Sheba," its interior goods; and "Seba," its exterior goods.

@Coro 41[2]. See <Arabia>.

Shechem.; Schechem.
See <Hamor>.

@AC 1401. "Shechem" = the Lord's second state.

@1440. "Abraham passed... to the place Shechem" (Genesis 12:6) = the Lord's second state, when the celestial things of love appeared to Him. Explained.

@1441. For Shechem is the first station in Canaan, in arriving from Syria; and as the land of Canaan = the celestial things of love, "Shechem" = the first appearing of celestial things.

@--. Jacob also came first to Shechem (Genesis 33), where "Shechem" = the first of light. Further illustrated.

@--[end]. Shechem being made a city of refuge (Joshua 20:7); a city of the priests (Joshua 21:21); and a covenant being made there (Joshua 24:1, 25) involve the like.

@4393. "Jacob came to Salem, the city of Shechem" (Genesis 33:18) = the interior truths of faith which are of tranquillity... "The city of Shechem" = the interior truths of faith.

@4430. "Shechem saw her" (Genesis 34:2) = truth; for "Shechem" = truth; here, the truth of the Church from Ancient [time]; because with that nation where Shechem was there were remains of the Church... Moreover the city Shechem was Abram's first station... Hence "Shechem" = the first of light; consequently, interior truth.

@--[3]. The city called after Shechem was anciently called Salem... but the same city was afterwards called Shechem. Illustrated. The same city was afterwards called Sychar. Illustrated.

@--[end]. That the city Shechem = interior truth. Illustrated.

@4436. "Shechem the son of Hamor" = the truth with the Ancients.

@4444[6]. This ancient statute was known to Shechem and Hamor... Thus Shechem was made such as a "sojourner," and so might have taken the daughter of Jacob, and therefore the killing of them was a nefarious deed.

@4448. "Shechem my son" (Genesis 34:8) = the truth from that good; for "Shechem" = interior truth, (which) in its essence is nothing but the good of charity; (for) the remains of the Most Ancient Church were with Hamor the Hivite, and his son Shechem. @4454.

@4453. To enter into the Knowledges of good and truth which are signified by Shechem the son of Hamor, and by his city. Signified.

@4454. "Shechem said to her father and brethren" (Genesis 34:11) = a consultation of the truth from an ancient Divine stock with the good and truth of this religiosity.

@4459. "Shechem" = the truth with the Ancients, or, what is the same, truth from an ancient Divine stock. @4476. @4477.

@4473. "Shechem," here (Genesis 34:18) = doctrine. Explained.

@4501. "Shechem" = the Church with the Ancients as to truth. References.

@4537[end]. "Oak near Shechem" = fallacious Natural.

@4707. "In Shechem" (Genesis 37:12) = first rudiments. "Shechem" = truth from an ancient Divine stock; doctrine; here, first rudiments of doctrine about faith. First rudiments are also generals of doctrinals: these are received first. @4709.

@4716. "(Joseph) came to Shechem" (Genesis 37:14) = Knowledge of generals of doctrinals. @4720.

@6306[7]. The city of Shechem is not meant.

@AE 374[6]. "Men from Shechem -Sichem-" (Jeremiah 41:5) = those who profane.

@638[23]. (Jotham's parable of the trees to the citizens of Shechem.)

Sheep.; Ovis.
See <Cattle-Pecus>, and <Flock>.

@AC 45. Sheep, mentioned.

@294[end]. "Sheep" = those gifted with the good of charity; that is, with spiritual and natural good.

@1361[2]. Lambs and sheep, sacrificed, = celestial things.

@2088[end]. Signification of the Lord's "other sheep." @2661[2]. @2669[end].

