@--[10]. "A ship of oar" (Isaiah 33:21) = intelligence from proprium, because propelled by men; "a magnificent ship" = wisdom from proprium... For "a ship" = intelligence and wisdom when it goes to sea and passes across; for so it is in its course, carrying wealth.

