@8364[2]. The spiritual life is sick when...

@8378. When the taste commands, the body is sick.

@9031[3]. Disease and sickness = the infirmity of the internal man...

@9242. Confidence, called faith, when they are sick.

@9324. When (truths and goods) are falsified and perverted, the man is sick...

@9780[8]. Therefore the sick were anointed with oil. @AE 375[43].

@10360[9]. The healing of the sick = the purification of man from evils and the falsities of evil.

@10758[2]. When they lie sick in bed... they believe they will live immediately after death.

@HH 470. When sick he thinks that Heaven is of pure mercy.

@571[2]. When this heat inflows into the sick, it excites insanities.

@DP 141. No one is reformed in a state of sickness of mind -animi-. Explained.

@142. When the body is sick, the mind -mens- is sick. Explained.

@CL 373. Jealousy from various sicknesses of the mind -mentis-.

@TCR 534. They who do not explore themselves are like a sick person...

@SE 4572[end]. Therefore the sick who ascribe the restoration of their health to the Lord, speak truly.

@4591. Spirits from such Hells are not present with the sick; but there is a general sphere and influx from such heats which is at once adopted by the disease itself.

@DMin 4586. "The sick" are those who are distressed by evils and falsities, and they are to be visited, by some who bring comfort, and by others who bring a remedy.

@4649. Under <Disease>, see this reference.

@4731. Such Spirits sometimes come to sick men, causing their death.

@AE 163[7]. "A sick person" = those who have transgressed and sinned; and therefore the Lord said to the sick man... "Sin no more..."

Sickle.; Falx.

@AC 1664[3]. "Beat their spears into pruninghooks" (Isaiah 2:4).

@9930[12]. "A sharp sickle" (Revelation 14:14) = the dispersion of evil and falsity. @AE 272[10]. ( = the Divine truth of the Word. Explained. @AR 643. @645. @646. @647. @649.) ( = the Divine truth exquisitely exploring and separating. @AE 908. @914.)

@AR 650. "The Angel put his sickle into the earth, and vintaged the vine of the earth" (Revelation 14:19) = the end of the present Christian Church.

@AE 911. To "put in the sickle" = to collect the good, and separate them from the evil.

Siddim.; Siddim.

@AC 1666. "The valley of Siddim" (Genesis 14:3) = the unclean things of cupidities. Explained.

@1684. "The valley of Siddim" (Genesis 14:8) = what is unclean.

@1688. "The valley of Siddim was full of pits of bitumen" (Genesis 14:10) = what is unclean of Falsities and cupidities; for "Siddim" = what is unclean.

Side.; Latus.
See <Part>.

@AC 537. A Spirit applied himself to my left side.

@1992[8]. The Spirits who rebuked were perceived at the side under the arm. @8021.

@3708[9]. All that is obscure as to good and truth is called "the sides of the earth."

@4189. Those at the side, are the gentiles (and their collateral good). Treated of.

@5356[end]. Evils and falsities rejected to the sides.

@5530. The things which do not agree with the loves are at the sides, and those which do not agree at all are rejected to the ultimate boundaries.

@5871. Then all the scientifics which are not congruous... are rejected from the middle to the sides; thus from the light which is in the middle to the shades which are at the sides.

@6068. The things not directly under the view are... at the sides.

@6386. "His side to Sidon" (Genesis 49:13) = extension on the one side -parte- to the Knowledges of good and truth. @AE 447[3]. @514[17].

@6479[end]. Any things they do not apprehend, they reject to the sides.

@6580[end]. (With such) the scientifics which confirm good and truth are rejected to the sides.

@7418. Places at the sides under the soles.

@7975. Then truths and goods not genuine are rejected to the sides. Signified.

@7976. They remain adjoined at the side.

@7984[2]. With the good, evil and falsity are rejected to the sides.

@8313[3]. "A great nation from the sides of the earth" (Jeremiah 6:22) = those who are in evils entirely opposite to good.

@9024[2]. "The sides of the earth" (Jeremiah 25:32) = where falsities from evil break out.

@9042[2]. "The sides of the earth from which they will be gathered" (Jeremiah 31:8) = where the truth and good of the Church begin; for "the earth" = the Church; and its "sides" are where are its first and its last.

@9081[2]. "With side and shoulder" = with all force and power.

@9164. Truths then depart to the sides, and make the circuit.

@9234. (The lunar Spirit who had been carried) applied himself to my left side under the elbow, and spoke thence.

@9495. Under <Ring>, see this reference.

@--[end]. "The side" = good which is to be conjoined with truth, and the derivative power.

@9496[2]. "The sides" (of the ark) relate to the thoracic part in man.

@9499. "Upon the sides of the ark" (Exodus 25:14) = in ultimates; for "the sides of the ark" = the Divine sphere which encompasses Heaven in ultimates; for the sides are the terminations, (which) in Heaven have no relation to spaces, but to goods conjoined with truths...

@9556. "Three reeds of the candlestick from its one side, and three... from its other side" (Exodus 25:32) = what is full as to good and truth... "From the one side and from the other side" = from good and the derivative truth; for the things on the right side of the body = goods, and those on the left side the truths thence; for instance, the right and left sides -partes- of the face.

@9663. "The side of the Habitation" (Exodus 26:26) = the quarter of Heaven whither the look is directed. Explained.

@9736. "The staves on the two sides of the altar" (Exodus 27:7) = the power of the good from which is truth, and of the truth from which is good. "The two sides" = good from truth and truth from good, thus the marriage of good with truth and of truth with good; because the things on the right side with man relate to good from which is truth, and those on the left side, to truth from good; for all the representatives in nature relate to the human form.

@10030[3]. "The belly and side" (Daniel 2:32) = the third state of the Church.

@10185. The "walls," or sides = interiors... For the sides and breast with man = interiors.

@10189. The sides, which are called "ribs" (Exodus 30:4), regard the south and north... but by sides, properly called sides, is signified good, because they regard the west and east. @10190.

@HH 223. At the right and left sides sit those in less light of wisdom.

@DLord 16[6]. Their "piercing His side" = that they had completely extinguished all the truth and good of the Word. @TCR 130[end].

@DLW 69[2]. He then relegates his fallacies to the sides.

@DP 279[2]. All things remain, and, when remitted after repentance, are moved out to the sides; and then... the things at the sides appear in shade, and sometimes in darkness.

@283. Still, evils... are only removed to the sides.

@284[2]. If good conquers, evil with its falsity is removed to the sides... If evil conquers, good with its truth is removed to the sides.

@CL 54[5]. Celibates are at the side of Heaven. Explained.

@235[end]. Merely natural Spirits become frigid when they apply themselves to the side of any Angel who is in a state of love.

@AE 175[9]. "The sides of the earth" = the things outside the Church; thus evils remote from the goods of the Church. @275[15]. ( = where are the ultimates of the Church, and where evils and falsities begin. @304[20].) ( = whence are evils; for "the sides of the earth" = what is remote from goods. @355[19].) ( = such ultimate truths. @721[10].)

@329[16]. His "side pierced, and blood and water coming out" (John 19:34, 35) = the conjunction of the Lord with the human race through the Divine truth proceeding from the Divine good of His love. For the breast = the Divine love; and "blood and water," the Divine truth proceeding.

@336[6]. "The side" at which a thousand shall fall (Psalms 91:7) = good.

@355[20]. "The sides of the north" (Ezekiel 38:15) = what is remote from goods and truths, thus whence are falsities of evil.

@365[39]. "The side" (Isaiah 66:12) = spiritual love.

@405[27]. "The sides of the north" (Psalms 48:2) = truths from celestial good.

@--[29]. "The sides of Lebanon" (Isaiah 37:24) = where these (goods) are conjoined with truths.

@560[end]. "As thorns in your sides" (Numbers 33:55)..."Sides" = the things of charity, thus goods.

@638[13]. "The house" = the spiritual mind; "its sides" (Psalms 128:3) = all things which are in the natural man.

@781[13]. "(The bear) raised itself up on its side" (Daniel 7:5) = the cupidity of falsifying the goods of the Word.

@1029[13]. "The sides of the pit" = places in Hell where are mere falsities of evil.

Sidon.; Sidon. Zidon.
Sidonian.; Sidonius.

