@9281[2]. The internal respiration is tacit.

@9587. Leading man so silently... @DP 186.

@DLW 382[2]. Therefore when a man thinks tacitly, he breathes tacitly.

@391[4]. The respiration of the spirit is so tacit that it is not perceived.

@404[3]. Meditation falls into the... tacit thought of the body.

@DP 183[2]. The Divine Providence takes away this evil silently.

@321[3]. These sometimes receive an answer by... a silent speech in the thought.

@CL 165. Women (then) are silent, and only listen.

@SE 1149. On those who want to speak silently, as if into the ear. @2371.

@2046. The speech of the deceitful is silent.

@2435. Spirits far from me hear and perceive better when I am thinking silently.

@3511. From the fact that they are silent... they derive the fact that they are invisible.

@5594. I have often spoken with Angels by a silent speech of ideas.

@AE 577[11]. Tacent, occurs.

Silfverstrom. @SE 4564. @5837.

Silk.; Sericum.

@AC 165[end]. Those not so innocent (as the naked) appear in garments... as of diamond-like silk.

@2576[10]. Its lower spiritual and doctrinal things are "garments of silk," etc. @5319[2]. @5620[4].

@5954[5]. "Fine linen and silk" (Ezekiel 16:10) = truths from good; but these [fabrics] in Heaven, being in its light, are resplendent and transparent.

@7601[7]. To "make flax of silk" (Isaiah 19:9) = to feign truths. ( = spiritual truth. @AE 654[50].)

@AR 773. "Silk," etc. (Revelation 18:12) = celestial goods and truths.

@CL 15. The prince wore a tunic of shining silk of a hyacinthine colour.

@42[3]. His shoes were all silk -holoserico-.

@137. They wore robes and tunics of refulgent silk, in which were inwoven flowers...

@TCR 74. Some with hats bound with silk, who were of the ecclesiastical order.

@102[3]. Mary appeared in white raiment as of silk.

@SE 6095. The African women appear in striped garments of silk (the men in the like of linen).

@AE 195[7]. "Fine linen and silk" = truths from a celestial origin. @1143[2].

@242[15]. "Fine linen" = genuine truth; "silk" = the same resplendent from interior good.

@619[11]. "Silk" = truth from a spiritual origin. @1144. @--[2], Explained.

@831[6]. Spiritual Angels (wear) fine linen and silk.

Silkworm.; Bombyx.

@DLW 61. Occurs. @DP 3[3]. @SE 3819.

@356. Those vile worms, called silkworms, clothe queens in silk... @CL 420. @TCR 13[3].

@TCR 335[4]. Does the silkworm, when a caterpillar, think in its little head...

@524[2]. The silkworm would perish... unless other worms were shaken off...

@687[3]. The wonderful transformation of silkworms, etc.

@785. It is the internal of the silkworm whereby its external is moved to spin silk.

Siloam.; Siloam. Siloah.

@AE 239[19]. "The pool of Siloam" (John 9) = the Word in the letter.

@475[17]. The waters of the lake or pool of Siloam = the truths of the Word.

Silver.; Argentum.
Silvern.; Argenteus.
See <Gold>.

@AC 113. "Silver" = truth. @424[end]. @2466[3]. @4677[9]. @4759. @6385. @9391[14]. @AR 772[end]. @AE 357[18]. @725[10]. @750[7].

@425. "Silver" = spiritual truth. @6432[2].

