@643. The inmost Spiritual they likened to silver.

@1197[4]. "Silver and gold" (Joel 3:5) = spiritual and celestial things of faith.

@1525. Rays of silvern light (with) those in affections of truth.

@1551. "(Abram rich) in silver" (Genesis 13:2) = the truths with which the Lord was enriched.

@--. The Most Ancients compared... the truths thence to silver.

@--[2]. That "silver," wherever mentioned, = truth; and, in the opposite, falsity. Illustrated.

@--. "He that hath no silver" (Isaiah 55:1) = one in ignorance of truth, yet in the good of charity, like many within and without the Church.

@--[4]. "Like silver purified seven times" (Psalms 12:6) = Divine truth. @AE 257[5].

@--[5]. "Gods of silver" = falsities.

@2048. "He that is bought with silver" (Genesis 17:12) = the spiritual... For "silver" = truth, thus what is spiritual of faith. @2114.

@2575. "A thousand of silver" (Genesis 20:16) = an infinite abundance of rational truth. @2576[7].

@2937. "In full silver" (Genesis 23:10) = redemption through truth. Explained. @2945. @2954. @2959. @2966.

@3021[8]. "Breast and arms of silver" (Daniel 2) = the second state of the Church, which was spiritual, because of charity. ( = spiritual good. @9406-7.) ( = truth from good. @10030[3].) @AE 176[2].

@3069[2]. To "drink waters for silver" (Lamentations 5:4) = to attribute truth to self. @AE 654[61].

@3079[2]. Under <Gold>, see this reference. @3154[2], etc., etc.

@3574[2]. "Molten image of their silver" (Hosea 13:2) = good falsified. ( = falsity ex quo. @AE 1186[2].)

@4099. "Hath devoured our silver" (Genesis 31:15) = consume the truth of these affections of truth. Explained.

@4453. If "silver" is mentioned in the Word, there is meant the truth which is of intelligence and of faith.

@5291[4]. "The silver hid in the earth" (Matthew 25:18) = the truth which is of faith (as used by one in faith without charity).

@5488. To "restore their silver" (Genesis 42:25) = without any power of theirs; for to "buy with silver" = to procure for one's self from what is one's own. @5496.

@5530. "Every one's bundle of his silver" (Genesis 42:35) = the ordinations of truths given gratis.

@5623. "Take double silver" (Genesis 43:12) = truth received (over again). Explained.

@5658. "Our silver in its weight" (Genesis 43:21) = truths according to the state of each.

@--[3]. When there is speech about truth, what is silvern appears there.

@--. With those who are in truth from truth, such things appear of silver.

@5660. "Other silver" (Genesis 43:22) = other truth. Explained.

@5664. a. "Your silver came to me" (Genesis 43:23) = it seems like truth procured by them.

@5735. "Put everyone's silver in his sack's mouth" (Genesis 44:1) = truth anew in the exterior Natural.

@5736. "My silver cup" (Genesis 44:2) = interior truth.

@5737. "And the silver of his corn" (id) = the truth of good.

@5955. To "Benjamin he gave 300 of silver" (Genesis 45:22) = what is full of truth from good.

@6112. "Joseph collected all the silver" (Genesis 47:14) = all the true and adaptable Scientific. @6115. @6116. @6119. @6122.

@6917. "Vessels of silver" (Exodus 3:22) = scientifics of truth. @7770.

@7999. "A purchase of silver" (Exodus 12:44) = one who has some spiritual truth.

@8764[7]. "Silver" = truth from good.

@9005. "Free without silver" (Exodus 21:11) = without truth conjoined with it.

@9039. "He is his silver" (Exodus 21:21) = truth acquired from proprium. Explained.

@9082. "30 shekels of silver" (Exodus 21:32) = restitution to the full through truth.

@9088. "He shall render silver" (Exodus 21:34) = (amendment) through truth. Explained. @AE 537[7].

@9093. "They shall divide the silver" (Exodus 21:35) = that its truth will be dispersed. Explained.

@9146[2]. "Silver" = truth of good; in the opposite, falsity of evil.

@9186. "He shall pay silver" (Exodus 22:17) = other truth consenting in its place. Explained.

@9209. "If thou shalt lend silver" (Exodus 22:25) = instruction. Explained.

@9424[6]. "Idols of silver" = falsities of doctrine.

@9643. "40 bases of silver" (Exodus 26:19) = plenary support through truth.

@9749. "Hooks... and fillets of silver" (Exodus 28:10) = modes of conjunction through truth.

@9852[end]. "Silver" = falsity.

@9881[end]. "Silver and gold from Tarshish" (Isaiah 60:9) = scientific truth and good.

@9960[4]. "Silver" = the truth which is of intelligence.

@10229. "The silver of expiations" (Exodus 30:16) = truths from good purifying.

@10332. "Silver" = interior and exterior truth.

@10355[3]. Silver = spiritual good, which in its essence is truth. @HH 115[end].

@10503. Idols of silver = worship of what is false in both doctrine and life.

@HH 185. Leaves as of silver.

@DSS 26[3]. Great purses full of silver seen, open, as if anyone might take of the silver. Explained.

@AR 459. "Idols of silver" (Revelation 9:20) = falsities about spiritual things.

@913. Silver (as a metal) corresponds to truths of wisdom.

