@14[end]. Dishes and plates of silver there.

@42[3]. Linen stockings with silver threads interwoven.

@76[end]. The vine leaves became silvern.

@156. [155a]. A white dove whose wings shone as from silver.

@TCR 609. Silver, sapphire, and vine, = spiritual good, which is the good of the Middle Heaven.

@SE 4045. Silver conveyed into my pocket.

@4732. While they acknowledge three Persons, their breastplate is silvern.

@4733. A sword with a silvern hilt is also given them.

@AE 70. "Silver," in the Word, = the truth (of celestial good) which is spiritual good.

@176. "Silver" = the truth (of the internal man). Illustrated.

@223[17]. To "buy fields with silver" (Jeremiah 32:44) = to procure for one's self the good of the Church through truths.

@236[4]. "Silver in thy treasuries" = Knowledges of truth.

@242[9]. "Silver" (Malachi 3:3) = truth from good.

@--[12]. "Silver" (Joel 3:5) = truth.

@--[16]. "Silver" (Isaiah 13:17) = the truth of the Church. @357[17]. @710[24].

@242[24]. "Silver," in the opposite, = falsity (from the evil of the love of self). Illustrated.

@279[9]. "Silver" = the truth which is from the Lord.

@283[4]. "Wings of a dove covered with silver" (Psalms 68:13) = spiritual truths.

@328[16]. To be "redeemed not by silver" (Isaiah 52:3) = that they cannot be emancipated from the falsities of evil through truth.

@365[41]. "Silver" (Isaiah 60:17) = the truth of (spiritual) good.

@433[14]. "My silver and My gold" (Joel 3:5) = the truths and goods of the Word.

@439[5]. "Plates of silver" (Psalms 68:30) = the truths of the Church. @627[13].

@447[4]. "Silver" (Judges 5:19) = truth from good.

@458[8]. "Silver" (Jeremiah 10:4) = truth (from the Word).

@539[12]. "Their silver" (Hosea 13:2) = what is from Own intelligence.

@540[6]. Things from the sense of the letter applied to themselves and their loves only, are called "dross of silver" (Ezekiel 22:18); for "silver" = the truth of the Word...

@585[10]. "Beaten out silver from Tarshish" (Jeremiah 10:9) = the truths of the Word in the sense of the letter. @587[6].

@587. A silvern idol = (false doctrine confirmed by the spiritual truth of the Word).

