Smooth.; Laevis.
Smoothness.; Laevitas.

@AC 3527. "I am a smooth man" (Genesis 27:11) = the quality of natural truth. Explained.

@AC 3527[2]. Hence those in natural truth were called smooth men.

@--. A mountain called the smooth -glaber seu laevis- mountain. Explained.

@--[3]. That "smooth" is predicated of truth; (or) falsity. Illustrated.

@--. "A smooth mouth" is predicated of falsity.

@3542. "Upon the smoothness of his neck" (Genesis 27:16) = that disjoining truth should not appear. "Smooth," or "smoothness" is predicated of truth.

