@3499. Wanted to snatch away their ideas.

@--. That they may pilfer their goods.

@--[end]. They now withdraw privily.

@3500[end]. As they can pilfer nothing from them, they have no commerce with them.

@3573. Evil Spirits snatch away truth and good. Explained.

@3701[end]. They snatch themselves away from sight.

@3883. They know how to snatch away an idea.

@3935. When I secretly took away the things they had used to destroy me.

@3980. When good works were snatched away from them.

@4239. Some would snatch away those being punished.

@4248. They would snatch away my thought.

Snorting.; Rhoncus.

@AE 355[31]. The confirmation of falsities thence is signified by "the snorting of his horses" (Jeremiah 8:16).

Snow.; Nix.
Snowy.; Niveus.

@AC 1042[2]. According to the varied mingling of dark and light.

@1774[2]. A face of snowy paleness.

@3412[3]. With such there appears a snowy light. @4416. @5128[3], Explained. @AE 1072.

@3812[4]. "Whiter than snow, and fairer than milk" (Lamentations 4:7) = in celestial truth. @AE 364[5].

@4007[2]. To "wash, and be made whiter than snow" (Psalms 51:7) = to be purified from sins by the reception and putting on of the Lord's righteousness.

@5060[2]. A little snowy one went out of his body, which represented their desire to put on a state of innocence. @4082.

@7626. The man of the Church is then like the earth covered with snow.

@7918[2]. "Snow" is predicated of truth. @8459, Illustrated.

@8952. Saturn's belt appears as a snowiness...

@9470[3]. "His garment as white as snow" (Daniel 7:9) = its external truth.

@10754[end]. Their noses are more of a snowy colour.

@HH 132. Truths outside the Heavens shine coldly, like what is snowy, without heat. @482[2]. Like winter, when all things lie under the snow.

@AR 47[end]. It is said "as wool, as snow" (Revelation 1:14) because... "snow" = truth in ultimates; for... snow is from water, which = truths of faith.

@ISB 6[4]. Spiritual light appears like resplendent and dazzling snow, such as His garments, when transfigured.

@TCR 185. In the frigid zones (there) snow appears on the lands... I was once led to a region where all the land appeared covered with snow. Described... The place of worship was unseen, because covered with snow. But the custodians were removing the snow, digging a way in.

@216. From its light (the Word) shines white like snow.

@SE 3430. He was shown naked and snowy. Explained.

@3468[end]. Their passive life is represented as of snowy light.

@3804. He emerged as a little snowy something like a man.

@3895. The girls appeared naked and snowy, which signified that they supposed themselves innocent.

@4012. He showed a snowy brain.

@4052[end]. The streets are very snowy, so that it appears a snowiness which = a life of faith.

@4074. The man clothed in what is snowy = those represented by Noah.

@4083. That snowiness then became black. Explained.

@4811. Nordberg appeared snowy as to the body and hands.

@5629. Under <England>, see this reference.

@5920. Melancthon's species of persuasion appeared snowy.

@DMin 4708. When this Hell was opened there appeared a striped snowiness. Explained.

@AE 67. "Snow" = truth in ultimates, because it is from water and from its whiteness.

@--[2]. That truth is described by "snow." Illustrated. @372[5]. @1042[8].

@411[28]. "The snow of Lebanon" = the truths of the Church thence. "Snow" here, = the like as water, namely, truths; but "snow" = cold truths, because such a Church is treated of.

@419[15]. "Snow and vapours" (Psalms 148:8) = the scientifics and Knowledges of the natural man; for these are "snow and vapour" before the man has become spiritual...

@475[11]. "Waters of snow" (Job 9:30) = truths which are, or which appear, genuine. @481[7].

@644[13]. "The snow coming down from heaven" (Isaiah 55:10) = natural truth (appropriated to man), which is like snow when only in the memory, but becomes spiritual through love, as snow becomes the water of rain by heat.

@704[2]. Under <Hail>, see this reference.

@798[4]. In the light of Heaven, their mind appears snowy, such as is rational light.

@1070[3]. "His garments as white as snow" = Divine truth.

@1208[end]. (Plant-like forms in snow. Explained.)

@DLove 17. 4. Still, their exteriors appear snowy and crimson from (external) uses.

